      "rev_n_1_9e39af_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_1_9e39af_1",
        "node_id": "n_1_9e39af",
        "thought_text": "Dynamic Programming Approach with Correct Initialization and State Transition\n\nInitialize the DP table such that `dp[i][j]` represents the number of ways to fill the grid up to the `i-th` row and `j-th` column with the given constraints. Use a dynamic programming approach where the state transition involves considering the minimum values required for rows and columns. Ensure correct initialization and boundary conditions to avoid off-by-one errors.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_1_9e39af_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_03c66401a3",
        "created_at": 1794502330.8310015
      },
      "rev_n_2_5aa06e_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_2_5aa06e_1",
        "node_id": "n_2_5aa06e",
        "thought_text": "Dynamic Programming Approach",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_2_5aa06e_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_2b87fefffa",
        "created_at": 1794502365.3570406
      },
      "rev_n_3_b09b63_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_3_b09b63_1",
        "node_id": "n_3_b09b63",
        "thought_text": "Graph Theory Representation\n\nRepresent the problem as a bipartite graph where one set of vertices represents rows and the other set represents columns. Each edge between a row vertex and a column vertex indicates that the corresponding cell in the grid can contain any value from 1 to k. Use Hall's Marriage Theorem to ensure that there exists a perfect matching, which corresponds to a valid way of filling the grid. Calculate the number of perfect matchings using dynamic programming on subsets.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_3_b09b63_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_b9a8ba2a6f",
        "created_at": 1794502432.6629581
      },
      "rev_n_4_f87e72_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_4_f87e72_0",
        "node_id": "n_4_f87e72",
        "thought_text": "Revisit the problem constraints and ensure proper initialization of the DP table.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-5455885644355621024",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794502457.3366287
      },
      "rev_n_5_528d13_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_5_528d13_0",
        "node_id": "n_5_528d13",
        "thought_text": "Consider using combinatorial mathematics to simplify the problem, focusing on choosing positions for the minimum values in each row and column.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-5455885644355621024",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794502457.336645
      },
      "rev_n_6_fa3fb5_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_6_fa3fb5_0",
        "node_id": "n_6_fa3fb5",
        "thought_text": "Implement a backtracking algorithm to explore all valid configurations of the grid while ensuring the constraints are met.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-5455885644355621024",
